<!-- IPC v1.x: VEHICE / VEHICLE (License Plate Recognition)
     Sent directly by the IP camera when a license plate is read.
     Shape observed on LPR-IP4 firmware 5.3.1 (HTTP POST V1 layout, config 1.7).
     Device identity, the timestamp, image data, and vehicle attribute values
     are placeholders. IB36NL is a test plate.

     smartType spelling depends on firmware:
       VEHICE  - firmware 5.1.1.0(52592) and 5.3.1
       VEHICLE - firmware 5.1.1.0(66800)
     alarmStatus field: vehiceAlarm

     Layout:
       No sourceDataInfo block. The overview image is listInfo item 0
       (image 0, empty plateNumber, width/height 0, empty targetType).
       listInfo item 1 holds the plate read and the plate crop
       (image 1, targetType "car").

     Plate item fields:
       plateNumber      - plate text
       vehicleDirect    - approach or away
       vehicleListType  - whiteList or blackList when the plate is on a list
                          (5.3.1). Absent when the plate is on no list.
                          Never sent on 5.1.x, even for listed plates.
       PlateConfidence  - value is in the count attribute, out of 10000
                          (9900 = 99%). The element has no text.
       plateColor       - numeric code in the count attribute (not a word)
       leftTop/rightTop/leftBottom/rightBottom - plate corners, 0-10000
       PlateWidth/PlateHeight - plate crop size in pixels
       carAttr          - vehicle color, type, brand, model (5.3.1)
       carRect          - vehicle box; y was an empty element on 5.3.1

     targetBase64Length is the length the camera declares. It did not match
     the actual base64 text on 5.3.1, so decode the text itself. -->
